    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265">

                <pb facs="0721" n="1535" xml:id="pg1535"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">330.13/10–1854: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France (Dillon) to the Department of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1954-10-18T19:00:00+01:00">October 18, 1954—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1634. Repeated information USUN 10 London 453.
                    Reference: Deptel 1418, October 16.<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d265-f1"/></p>
                <p>Department’s concern as indicated reference telegram conveyed frankly to
                        Parodi<anchor n="2" xml:id="d265-f2"/> today. He
                    replied immediately Moch was acting on
                    his own as usual and was difficult to control. He said
                        Mendes<anchor n="3" xml:id="d265-f3"/> had yesterday
                    been irritated with Moch over an
                    article in <hi rendition="#italic">London Observer</hi> (which we have not been
                    able to identify) and had sent him a sharp telegram last night. In response to
                    our inquiry as to what might be done to control Moch, Parodi said he did not know but would
                    consult Mendes. He also suggested that I take it up
                    directly with latter which I will do at first opportunity.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Dillon</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d265-f1" n="1" xml:id="d265-f1-content">
                <p><hi rendition="#italic">Supra</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d265-f2" n="2" xml:id="d265-f2-content">
                <p>Alexandre Parodi, Secretary General of the French Ministry
                    of Foreign Affairs.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d265-f3" n="3" xml:id="d265-f3-content">
                <p>Pierre Mendès-France, Premier of France.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
